From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] What people see says no "Wine" (5970)

Window titles, error boxes and device names people meet said "Wine":
the old browser's frame and its message boxes ("Wine Internet Explorer"),
Help ("Wine Help", old programs' .hlp files), the C runtime's error box
("Wine C++ Runtime Library ... start the Wine debugger"), the sound
mapper in programs' audio device lists ("Wine Sound Mapper"), File
Manager, WordPad, the uninstaller, regsvr32's usage box, Internet
settings' description, explorer's browser window. Each says its plain
name, as Windows' do. The desktop window keeps "<name> - Wine Desktop":
nobody sees it and the compositor knows it by it.

Gate test/progname-gate.sh.
